/*?
 * Text: "entry %i: %s (addr=0x%lx size=%lu)\n"
 * Severity: Informational
 * Parameter:
 *   @1: ID of the OS info entry
 *   @2: Entry state (e.g "copied" or "not available")
 *   @3: Address of the entry
 *   @4: Size of the entry
 * Description:
 * Linux is running in kdump mode and reports information on OS info entries
 * defined by the old kernel. Possible values for "entry state" are:
 * - copied: The entry has been found, verified, and copied
 * - not available: The old kernel has not defined the entry
 * - checksum failed: The entry is corrupt
 * User action:
 * If kdump fails, send the messages to your service organization.
 */

